sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    title Workflow 3 (research extension): Adaptive thread pool resizing
    participant Mon as Monitor thread
    participant Q as Shared request buffer
    participant P as Pool state<br/>(pool mutex: n_workers, n_idle, retire_target, spawn_rate)
    participant NW as New worker(s)
    participant IW as Idle worker

    loop every sampling interval (e.g. 50 ms)
        Mon->>Q: lock, read queue length q, unlock
        Mon->>P: lock, read n_workers and n_idle, unlock
        alt q > high watermark for k samples in a row AND n_workers < max
            Mon->>P: lock, add = min(spawn_rate, max - n_workers), n_workers += add, unlock
            loop add times
                Mon->>NW: pthread_create(worker_loop)
            end
            NW->>Q: lock, wait(not_empty) or take a request
            Mon->>P: lock, spawn_rate = min(spawn_rate * 2, SPAWN_CAP), unlock
            Note over Mon,NW: Grow fast: add 1, 2, 4, ... threads per round while the queue stays long<br/>(same idea as Apache httpd's idle_spawn_rate)
        else n_idle > 0 AND q == 0 for a longer window AND n_workers > min
            Mon->>P: lock, retire_target++, spawn_rate = 1, unlock
            Mon->>Q: broadcast(not_empty)
            IW->>Q: wakes up, sees count == 0
            IW->>P: lock, retire_target > 0, so retire_target--, n_workers--, unlock
            IW->>IW: unlock buffer, pthread_exit()
            Note over Mon,IW: Shrink slowly: retire only 1 thread per round (hysteresis) so the pool does not flap
        else otherwise
            Mon->>P: lock, spawn_rate = 1, unlock
            Mon->>Mon: keep current size
        end
        Mon->>Mon: log (time, q, n_workers) for the thread-count plot
    end
